new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..8b72d1e3ff4fdbf12f563fb86cbf5f2303a04b7a
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/run-commands.md
@@ -0,0 +1,57 @@
+# Run command admission
+
+`GET /api/v1/runs/:runId/command-context` observes the current source status,
+opaque Session head and current authority stamp. `POST .../commands` atomically
+creates a queued successor, immutable command receipt and one
+`run.command.created` event on that successor. The predecessor's Run, events,
+messages, usage and receipts remain unchanged.
+
+| Kind | Source status | Input | Relation | Task root |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| retry | failed | Original logical request | retry_of | Inherited |
+| resume | cancelled, expired | Original logical request | continues | Inherited |
+| continue | Any terminal status | Explicit new input | continues | Successor |
+
+A pending permission is not a terminal source. Resolve its exact permission
+through the existing permission endpoint and attempt/worker/lease fence.
+
+The body is `{command, input?}` for ordinary requests. The command has exactly
+`version:1`, `commandId`, `sourceRunId`, `kind`, `expectedSessionHead`,
+`expectedSourceStatus`, `expectedAuthoritySha256`, and `expiresAt`. Only continue
+accepts/requires `input`. The deadline must be within 120 seconds at admission.
+
+Signed Work Runtime requests preserve the existing canonical packet unchanged in
+`{input:[packetText], command}`. The HTTP path/body and fresh operation context,
+correlation and idempotency key are signed. Current actor, binding, original role,
+policy, signing key and prepared deployment are rechecked inside the transaction.
+Recovery requires the same signed operation context/request/correlation proof.
+The original receipt's context is still required for ordinary protected Run reads.
+This does not grant an observer credential control authority.
+
+Same actor/command ID with the same full intent returns the original receipt;
+different intent returns 409. Distinct IDs observing one Session head cannot both
+admit successors. Active Runs, changed head/status and expiry create durable
+rejected receipts. Ordinary enqueue remains fenced by the active-Run constraint.
+Accepted receipt source/successor/root references have scoped foreign keys.
+Rejected attempts retain the checked source identity without waiting on an active
+worker's Run row lock. Session authorization and scope checks still apply.
+
+`GET /api/v1/sessions/:sessionId/commands/:commandId` returns `found` with the
+original positive receipt, or `not_found`. It rechecks current authority; no stored
+receipt bypasses revocation. A lost COMMIT acknowledgement is `503 outcome_unknown`.
+Recover the same command ID before any further user decision. Do not create a new
+key or infer acceptance from an unrelated Run.
+
+New accepted admission is HTTP202; accepted replay is HTTP200; durable rejection
+is HTTP409. Acceptance means queued admission, not execution success, external
+effects rollback or completion of the parent Task. Native receipt resources omit
+actor, authority/input hashes, recovery proof, input and credentials.
+
+Ordinary personal provider authorization retains its original connection pin.
+Deployment-pinned execution instead requires its current deployment settings and
+availability; unrelated personal login rotation does not change that authority.
+
+Migration027 and these endpoints have only been exercised in isolated PostgreSQL
+QA. Operating processes/databases have not been upgraded. Assistant WorkCoordinator
+attempt/ref integration and Track control/recovery UI remain separate work; sending
+a native successor alone does not implement a failed coordinator-role retry.
